  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "Cindy was asked by her teacher to subtract \\(3\\) from a certain number and then divide the result by \\(9.\\) Instead, she subtracted \\(9\\) and then divided the result by \\(3,\\) giving an answer of \\(43.\\) What would her answer have been had she worked the problem correctly?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(15\\)",
    "B": "\\(34\\)",
    "C": "\\(43\\)",
    "D": "\\(51\\)",
    "E": "\\(138\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Undo Cindy’s operations in reverse order to recover the original number. Her last step divided by \\(3\\) and produced \\(43\\), so the number just before division was\n\\[\n43\\cdot3=129.\n\\]\nShe obtained \\(129\\) by subtracting \\(9\\), so the original number was \\(129+9=138\\).\n\nNow carry out the intended operations: subtract \\(3\\), then divide by \\(9\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{138-3}{9}=\\frac{135}{9}=\\boxed{15}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
